IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `lt-common`

-- Local Government (Rates and Charges Remissions) Act 1991 (Tas), read with the Local Government (Rates and Charges
-- Remissions) Regulations 2024 (Tas) -- the seat-neutral core. Encoded here, in the Land Tax Act 2000's folder, beside
-- the land tax rules (see NOTES.md).
--
-- Rules in the Act's own actors and terms: the eligible pensioner who applies, the municipality, the person given a
-- remission, the surviving spouse, the Commissioner of State Revenue and the objector. Where the text says "must" or
-- sets a deadline, the rule is regulative. The pensioner's questions are asked in lta-seat.l4.
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED: s 3 (charges, rates, eligible pensioner, spouse); s 4(1)-(9); s 4A; s 4B; s 4C; s 4E; s 4F;
-- Regulations 2024 regs 4, 5, 6.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: s 4D (an objection out of time: by the Commissioner's permission, as a note only); ss 4G-4I
-- (investigations); ss 5, 6 (the Treasurer's reimbursement of the municipality and directions); s 8.
--
-- Edition: Act consolidation published 2019-05-23 (../../../local-government-rates-and-charges-remissions-act-1991/
-- registers/source-bundle/act-1991-008.txt); Regulations 2024 version published 2024-10-16
-- (../../../local-government-rates-and-charges-remissions-regulations-2024/registers/source-bundle/sr-2024-055.txt);
-- both current at 2026-10-20. The reg 5(2) formula is shown in the source as an image and was transcribed at deposit as
-- "A = B x (C / D)". Copyright State of Tasmania, CC BY 4.0. Based on material from the Tasmanian Legislation website at
-- 20 October 2026. For the latest information on Tasmanian Government legislation please go to
-- www.legislation.tas.gov.au.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Local Government (Rates and Charges Remissions) Act 1991 and Regulations 2024 -- the core`

§§ `reg 4 -- eligible pensioner`

-- reg 4(2): "eligible pensioner means -- (a) a person who holds a current pensioner concession card; or (b) a person
-- who holds a current pensioner concession card that is for the time being inoperative because the person is
-- temporarily out of Australia; or (c) a person who holds a current health care card; or (d) a totally and
-- permanently incapacitated person; or (e) a war widow; or (f) a war widower."
-- reg 4(1): "pensioner concession card means a pensioner concession card issued under the Social Security Act 1991 of
-- the Commonwealth or as a fringe benefit under the Veterans' Entitlements Act 1986"; "health care card means a health
-- care card -- (a) within the meaning of the Social Security Act 1991 ...; and (b) issued to a person eligible under
-- that Act"; "totally and permanently incapacitated person means a person to whom section 24 of the Veterans'
-- Entitlements Act 1986 ..., or section 199 of the Military Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2004 ..., applies";
-- "war widow" and "war widower": "(a) ... receiving a pension under Part II or IV of the Veterans' Entitlements Act 1986
-- ... at a rate determined in accordance with section 30(1) of that Act; or (b) a person who was a wholly dependent
-- partner of a person who is a deceased member, within the meaning of section 5 of the Military Rehabilitation and
-- Compensation Act 2004 ..., to whom section 12 of that Act applies". These Commonwealth terms are facts.
-- READING (finding 15): since (b) adds a card that is inoperative while the holder is abroad, (a) is read as a card in
-- operation.
DECLARE `Cards and pensions` HAS
    `holds a current pensioner concession card in operation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `holds a current pensioner concession card inoperative only because temporarily out of Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
    `holds a current health care card` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a person to whom VEA s 24 or MRCA s 199 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
    `receives a war widow's or widower's pension under VEA Part II or IV at the s 30(1) rate` IS A BOOLEAN
    `was the wholly dependent partner of a deceased member to whom MRCA s 12 applies` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the person` IS A `Cards and pensions`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an eligible pensioner under reg 4` IF
        `the person`'s `holds a current pensioner concession card in operation`
    OR  `the person`'s `holds a current pensioner concession card inoperative only because temporarily out of Australia`
    OR  `the person`'s `holds a current health care card`
    OR  `the person`'s `is a person to whom VEA s 24 or MRCA s 199 applies`
    OR  `the person`'s `receives a war widow's or widower's pension under VEA Part II or IV at the s 30(1) rate`
    OR  `the person`'s `was the wholly dependent partner of a deceased member to whom MRCA s 12 applies`

§§ `s 4(3)-(3C) and reg 6 -- occupying the property as a principal dwelling`

-- reg 6: "the following are prescribed institutions: (a) a residential facility providing residential care as defined
-- in section 41-3 of the Aged Care Act 1997 of the Commonwealth; (b) a hospital providing care to nursing-home type
-- patients as defined in section 3 of the Health Insurance Act 1973 of the Commonwealth; (c) a facility providing
-- psychiatric or psychological care to persons residing in the facility." (finding 18: the Aged Care Act 1997 was
-- repealed from 1 November 2025.)
DECLARE `Where a person lives on 1 July` IS ONE OF
    `in the property, as their principal dwelling`
    `in a residential care facility under the Aged Care Act 1997 s 41-3`
    `in a hospital as a nursing-home type patient under the Health Insurance Act 1973 s 3`
    `in a facility providing residential psychiatric or psychological care`
    `somewhere else`

GIVEN `the place` IS A `Where a person lives on 1 July`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is in a prescribed institution under reg 6` IF
    CONSIDER `the place`
    WHEN `in a residential care facility under the Aged Care Act 1997 s 41-3` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `in a hospital as a nursing-home type patient under the Health Insurance Act 1973 s 3` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `in a facility providing residential psychiatric or psychological care` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 4(3): "a person is taken to have been occupying a property as a principal dwelling on 1 July in a financial year if
-- -- (a) in the case of a single person, that person was in a prescribed institution and did not receive any rental
-- income from the property; or (b) in the case of a person who is married or in a significant relationship ... -- (i)
-- that person and that person's spouse were in a prescribed institution and neither person received any rental income
-- from the property; or (ii) that person was in a prescribed institution and that person's spouse occupied the property
-- as his or her principal place of residence."
-- s 4(3A), (3B): for (3)(a) and (3)(b)(i) "a person must provide a statutory declaration" that they (and the spouse)
-- were in a prescribed institution and received no rental income.
-- s 4(3C): "A person referred to in subsection (3)(a) or subsection (3)(b)(i) is only eligible for a remission of rates
-- or charges for a period not exceeding 2 consecutive financial years." READING (finding 17): the year asked about and
-- the years remitted in a row on that footing just before it count; the third in a row is refused.
DECLARE `Occupation on 1 July` HAS
    `where the person lives` IS A `Where a person lives on 1 July`
    `is married or in a significant relationship` IS A BOOLEAN
    `where the spouse lives` IS A `Where a person lives on 1 July`
    `the person or the spouse received rental income from the property` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a statutory declaration under s 4(3A) or (3B) has been provided` IS A BOOLEAN
    `consecutive financial years just before this one remitted while in an institution under s 4(3)(a) or (b)(i)` IS A NUMBER

`the most consecutive years remitted under s 4(3)(a) or (b)(i)` MEANS 2

GIVEN `the occupation` IS AN `Occupation on 1 July`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 4(3C) limit is not reached` IF
    `the occupation`'s `consecutive financial years just before this one remitted while in an institution under s 4(3)(a) or (b)(i)` PLUS 1
        AT MOST `the most consecutive years remitted under s 4(3)(a) or (b)(i)`

GIVEN `the occupation` IS AN `Occupation on 1 July`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is occupying the property as a principal dwelling under s 4` IF
    IF `the occupation`'s `where the person lives` EQUALS `in the property, as their principal dwelling`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE IF `is in a prescribed institution under reg 6` (`the occupation`'s `where the person lives`)
         THEN IF `the occupation`'s `is married or in a significant relationship`
              THEN     `the occupation`'s `where the spouse lives` EQUALS `in the property, as their principal dwelling`
                   OR  (    `is in a prescribed institution under reg 6` (`the occupation`'s `where the spouse lives`)
                        AND (NOT (`the occupation`'s `the person or the spouse received rental income from the property`))
                        AND `the occupation`'s `a statutory declaration under s 4(3A) or (3B) has been provided`
                        AND `the s 4(3C) limit is not reached` `the occupation`)
              ELSE     (NOT (`the occupation`'s `the person or the spouse received rental income from the property`))
                   AND `the occupation`'s `a statutory declaration under s 4(3A) or (3B) has been provided`
                   AND `the s 4(3C) limit is not reached` `the occupation`
         ELSE FALSE

§§ `s 4(1)-(1D) -- applying, granting and the years remitted`

-- s 4(1): "An eligible pensioner who is liable to pay rates or charges to a municipality (or, if there is more than one
-- such person, one of them) may apply to the municipality before 31 March in a financial year for a 30% remission on
-- those rates or charges for -- (a) the financial year in which the application was made; and (b) all subsequent
-- financial years." "Before 31 March": the last day is 30 March (finding 14).
`the remission rate` MEANS 30%

GIVEN `the financial year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to apply in the financial year` MEANS YMD (`the financial year` PLUS 1) 3 30

GIVEN `the day of application` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the application is made before 31 March in its financial year` IF
    `is on or before` `the day of application` (`the last day to apply in the financial year` (`the financial year of` `the day of application`))

DECLARE `Application` HAS
    `the day of application` IS A DATE
    `the applicant is an eligible pensioner when applying` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the applicant is liable to pay rates or charges to the municipality` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the application` IS AN `Application`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an application under s 4(1)` IF
        `the application`'s `the applicant is an eligible pensioner when applying`
    AND `the application`'s `the applicant is liable to pay rates or charges to the municipality`
    AND `the application is made before 31 March in its financial year` (`the application`'s `the day of application`)

-- s 4(1A): "On receipt of an application, a municipality is to grant the application if on 1 July in the financial
-- year in which the application was made the applicant was -- (a) an eligible pensioner; and (b) occupying as his or
-- her principal dwelling the property in respect of which the rates or charges are payable."
GIVEN `the application` IS AN `Application`, `eligible pensioner on that 1 July` IS A BOOLEAN, `occupying on that 1 July` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the municipality is to grant the application under s 4(1A)` IF
        `is an application under s 4(1)` `the application`
    AND `eligible pensioner on that 1 July`
    AND `occupying on that 1 July`

-- s 4(1B): on granting, the municipality "is to remit 30% of any rates or charges payable to it by the applicant for --
-- (a) the financial year in which the application was made; and (b) each subsequent financial year until the applicant
-- is no longer eligible for the remission." (1C): "no longer eligible ... if on 1 July in a subsequent financial year he
-- or she is no longer -- (a) an eligible pensioner; or (b) occupying as his or her principal dwelling the property".
-- (1D): "If an eligible pensioner makes an application under subsection (1), a municipality is to remit 30% of any rates
-- or charges paid or payable to it by the applicant for the financial year immediately preceding the financial year in
-- which the application was made if on 1 July in that immediately preceding financial year the applicant was -- (a) an
-- eligible pensioner; and (b) occupying as his or her principal dwelling the property".
-- READING (finding 16): once (1C) ends the remission it does not revive; a fresh application is needed.
DECLARE `Remission history` HAS
    `the application` IS AN `Application`
    `the application was granted under s 4(1A)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `eligible pensioner and occupying on 1 July of the year before the application` IS A BOOLEAN
    `eligible pensioner and occupying on every 1 July after the year of the application, up to the year asked about` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the history` IS A `Remission history`, `the financial year asked about` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the financial year is remitted under s 4(1B)-(1D)` IF
    IF `the financial year asked about` EQUALS `the year of the application`
    THEN `the history`'s `the application was granted under s 4(1A)`
    ELSE IF `the financial year asked about` EQUALS `the year of the application` MINUS 1
         THEN     `is an application under s 4(1)` (`the history`'s `the application`)
              AND `the history`'s `eligible pensioner and occupying on 1 July of the year before the application`
         ELSE IF `the financial year asked about` GREATER THAN `the year of the application`
              THEN     `the history`'s `the application was granted under s 4(1A)`
                   AND `the history`'s `eligible pensioner and occupying on every 1 July after the year of the application, up to the year asked about`
              ELSE FALSE
    WHERE
        `the year of the application` MEANS `the financial year of` (`the history`'s `the application`'s `the day of application`)

§§ `s 4(2) and reg 5 -- the maximum remission`

-- s 4(2): "The amount remitted by a municipality under this section for rates or charges payable in respect of a
-- property for a financial year must not exceed the prescribed amount relevant to that financial year."
-- reg 5(4): "the maximum amount that may be remitted for the 2024-2025 financial year is -- (a) $379.41 in relation to
-- an area of land, the owner or occupier of which is a customer within the meaning of the Water and Sewerage Industry
-- Act 2008; and (b) $558.50 in relation to an area of land, the owner or occupier of which is not a customer".
`the first financial year of the 2024 Regulations` MEANS 2024

GIVEN `a water and sewerage customer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the 2024-25 maximum remission` MEANS
    IF `a water and sewerage customer` THEN 379.41 ELSE 558.50

-- reg 5(5): "An amount which is a fraction of a cent is rounded to the nearest cent by -- (a) where the number is 0.5 of
-- a cent or more, increasing that amount to the next whole cent; or (b) where the number is less than 0.5 of a cent,
-- decreasing that amount". (6): to the nearest dollar, "where the number of cents is 50 or more, increasing ... ; or
-- ... less than 50, decreasing".
GIVEN `amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`rounded to the nearest cent under reg 5(5)` MEANS FLOOR (`amount` TIMES 100 PLUS 0.5) DIVIDED BY 100

GIVEN `amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`rounded to the nearest dollar under reg 5(6)` MEANS FLOOR (`amount` PLUS 0.5)

-- reg 5(1): "CPI figure means the Consumer Price Index (All Groups) Number for Hobart published by the Australian
-- Statistician"; "March quarter, in relation to a financial year, means the months of January, February and March in
-- that financial year."
-- reg 5(2): A = B x (C / D), where "A is the maximum amount that may be remitted for the financial year, rounded to the
-- nearest cent ... and then rounded to the nearest dollar ...; B is the maximum amount, before rounding, that could be
-- remitted in the financial year immediately preceding ...; C is the CPI figure for the March quarter of the financial
-- year immediately preceding the financial year in which the maximum amount is to apply; D is the CPI figure for the
-- March quarter immediately preceding the March quarter referred to in the definition of C."
-- reg 5(3): "If the maximum amount A ... is less than the maximum amount for the preceding year, the maximum amount that
-- may be remitted is to remain the same as the preceding year."
-- The CPI figures are inputs, in order from the March quarter 2024 (in 2023-24): for 2025-26, C is March 2025 and D is
-- March 2024. READING (finding 12): where reg 5(3) keeps the preceding year's maximum, the amount "before rounding" that
-- B carries into the next year is the preceding year's too.
DECLARE `Maximum for a year` HAS
    `before rounding` IS A NUMBER
    `the maximum` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the base` IS A NUMBER, `years after 2024-25` IS A NUMBER, `the CPI figures` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A `Maximum for a year`
`the maximum under reg 5` MEANS
    IF `years after 2024-25` AT MOST 0
    THEN `Maximum for a year` WITH
             `before rounding` IS `the base`
             `the maximum`     IS `the base`
    ELSE IF `A` LESS THAN `the preceding year`'s `the maximum`
         THEN `the preceding year`
         ELSE `Maximum for a year` WITH
                  `before rounding` IS `B times C over D`
                  `the maximum`     IS `A`
    WHERE
        `the preceding year` MEANS `the maximum under reg 5` `the base` (`years after 2024-25` MINUS 1) `the CPI figures`
        `B times C over D` MEANS
            `the preceding year`'s `before rounding` TIMES (at `the CPI figures` `years after 2024-25`) DIVIDED BY (at `the CPI figures` (`years after 2024-25` MINUS 1))
        `A` MEANS `rounded to the nearest dollar under reg 5(6)` (`rounded to the nearest cent under reg 5(5)` `B times C over D`)

GIVEN `the financial year` IS A NUMBER, `a water and sewerage customer` IS A BOOLEAN, `the CPI figures` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Amount answer`
`the prescribed maximum remission for` MEANS
    IF `the financial year` LESS THAN `the first financial year of the 2024 Regulations`
    THEN `not covered` `the financial year begins before 1 July 2024: the maximum remission for it is set by regulations that are not deposited (the 2024 Regulations start from 2024-25)`
    ELSE IF count `the CPI figures` LESS THAN `the financial year` MINUS `the first financial year of the 2024 Regulations` PLUS 1
         THEN `not covered` `a Hobart CPI figure that the year's maximum remission needs was not given`
         ELSE `the amount, in dollars, is` (`the year's figures`'s `the maximum`)
    WHERE
        `the year's figures` MEANS
            `the maximum under reg 5` (`the 2024-25 maximum remission` `a water and sewerage customer`) (`the financial year` MINUS `the first financial year of the 2024 Regulations`) `the CPI figures`

-- s 3: "rates means rates payable under Part 9 of the Local Government Act 1993 and, if a discount has been given, means
-- the amount of rates actually paid, but does not include any penalty or interest charges"; "charges" likewise.
-- s 4(1B) with s 4(2): 30% of the rates and charges, but not more than the prescribed maximum. The Act sets no rounding
-- for the 30%.
GIVEN `the rates and charges` IS A NUMBER, `the maximum` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount remitted under s 4(1B) and (2)` MEANS
    `the lesser of` (`the rates and charges` TIMES `the remission rate`) `the maximum`

§§ `s 4(4)-(8) -- the surviving spouse`

-- s 4(4): "If -- (a) an eligible pensioner who would be entitled to make an application under subsection (1) for a
-- remission of rates or charges payable in respect of a property dies without making that application but leaves a
-- surviving spouse; and (b) the surviving spouse is occupying the property on 1 July in the financial year in which the
-- application could have been made -- the surviving spouse may make that application." (5): it "shall have effect as
-- if it were an application made under subsection (1) by an eligible pensioner." (6): the remission "may only be given
-- in respect of the financial year in which the application is made and, if subsection (1D) applies, the financial year
-- immediately preceding" and is given to the surviving spouse. s 3: "spouse includes the person with whom a person is,
-- or was at the time of his or her death, in a significant relationship".
GIVEN `the pensioner would have been entitled to apply` IS A BOOLEAN, `the pensioner died without applying` IS A BOOLEAN, `the surviving spouse occupies the property on 1 July of that year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the surviving spouse may apply under s 4(4)` IF
        `the pensioner would have been entitled to apply`
    AND `the pensioner died without applying`
    AND `the surviving spouse occupies the property on 1 July of that year`

GIVEN `the year of the spouse's application` IS A NUMBER, `the financial year asked about` IS A NUMBER, `s 4(1D) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a surviving spouse's application can cover the year under s 4(6)` IF
        `the financial year asked about` EQUALS `the year of the spouse's application`
    OR  (`s 4(1D) applies` AND `the financial year asked about` EQUALS `the year of the spouse's application` MINUS 1)

-- s 4(7): if the eligible pensioner who applied "dies in the financial year in which that application was made", would
-- have been entitled to a remission "for that financial year or the immediately preceding financial year, or both", and
-- "a surviving spouse ... was occupying the property on 1 July in that financial year -- the municipality is to give any
-- unpaid remission for that financial year and the immediately preceding financial year, if relevant, to the surviving
-- spouse." (8): if the pensioner "dies in a financial year subsequent to the financial year in which the application was
-- made", would have been entitled for "that subsequent financial year", and the spouse was occupying the property on 1
-- July in that subsequent financial year, the municipality "is to give any unpaid remission for that subsequent
-- financial year to that surviving spouse."
GIVEN `the year of the application` IS A NUMBER, `the year of death` IS A NUMBER, `the financial year asked about` IS A NUMBER, `the pensioner would have been entitled for the year asked about` IS A BOOLEAN, `the surviving spouse occupied the property on 1 July of the year of death` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the surviving spouse is to be given the unpaid remission under s 4(7)-(8)` IF
        `the pensioner would have been entitled for the year asked about`
    AND `the surviving spouse occupied the property on 1 July of the year of death`
    AND (    (    `the year of death` EQUALS `the year of the application`
              AND (    `the financial year asked about` EQUALS `the year of the application`
                   OR  `the financial year asked about` EQUALS `the year of the application` MINUS 1))
         OR  (    `the year of death` GREATER THAN `the year of the application`
              AND `the financial year asked about` EQUALS `the year of death`))

§§ `ss 4(9), 4A, 4B-4F -- notices, false statements, repayment and review`

-- s 4(9): "A person given a remission on rates or charges under this section for a financial year must notify a
-- municipality in writing before the end of that financial year if he or she ceases to -- (a) be an eligible pensioner;
-- or (b) occupy as his or her principal dwelling the property in respect of which the remission on rates or charges was
-- given. Penalty: ... a fine not exceeding 2 penalty units." "Before the end of that financial year": by 30 June.
`the most penalty units for an offence against s 4(9)` MEANS 2

GIVEN `the financial year of the remission` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to notify the municipality under s 4(9)` MEANS `30 June ending` `the financial year of the remission`

-- s 4A: "A person must not, in giving any information under this Act -- (a) make a statement knowing it to be false or
-- misleading; or (b) omit any matter from a statement knowing that without that matter the statement is false or
-- misleading. Penalty: Fine not exceeding 2 penalty units."
`the most penalty units for an offence against s 4A` MEANS 2

-- s 4C(2)(b): an objection to a s 4B decision is lodged "within 60 days after the objector receives a written notice
-- under section 4B" (or later with the Commissioner's permission under s 4D). s 4F(2): "An application for a review
-- must be made within 60 days after the objector receives a written notice under section 4E(2)" -- to the Magistrates
-- Court (Administrative Appeals Division) (s 4F(1)).
`the days to object under s 4C` MEANS 60

`the days to apply for review under s 4F` MEANS 60

§§ `Regulative rules -- the applicant, the municipality, the person given the remission and the Commissioner`

-- Clock: days, counted from the day the rule starts (stated with each rule).

-- s 4(1), (1A): the eligible pensioner may apply before 31 March; on an application the municipality "is to grant" it
-- if the 1 July conditions held. Clock starts on 1 July of the financial year; the seat works out the days to 30 March.
-- Not applying is no breach. No period binds the municipality.
GIVEN `days from 1 July to the last day to apply` IS A NUMBER, `the 1 July conditions of s 4(1A) were met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Step`
DECIDE `s 4(1), (1A) -- the eligible pensioner may apply before 31 March, and the municipality is to grant the remission` IS
    PARTY `the applicant`
    DO    `apply to the municipality for the remission`
    WITHIN `days from 1 July to the last day to apply`
    HENCE (IF `the 1 July conditions of s 4(1A) were met`
           THEN PARTY `the municipality`
                MUST  `remit 30% of the rates and charges, up to the prescribed maximum`
           ELSE FULFILLED)
    LEST  FULFILLED

-- s 4(9): notice in writing before the end of the financial year. Clock starts on the day the person ceases to be an
-- eligible pensioner or to occupy the property; the seat works out the days to 30 June.
GIVEN `the person ceased to be eligible or to occupy the property` IS A BOOLEAN, `days from ceasing to the end of the financial year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Step`
DECIDE `s 4(9) -- the person given the remission must notify the municipality before the end of the year` IS
    IF `the person ceased to be eligible or to occupy the property`
    THEN PARTY `the person given the remission`
         MUST  `notify the municipality in writing`
         WITHIN `days from ceasing to the end of the financial year`
         LEST  BREACH BY `the person given the remission` BECAUSE "s 4(9): a person given a remission must notify the municipality in writing before the end of the financial year on ceasing to be an eligible pensioner or to occupy the property; fine not exceeding 2 penalty units"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- s 4A: a prohibition while information is being given under the Act. Clock starts when the person begins giving the
-- information; it runs for the days stated.
GIVEN `days over which the information is given` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Step`
DECIDE `s 4A -- the applicant must not make a false or misleading statement` IS
    PARTY `the applicant`
    SHANT `make a statement known to be false or misleading`
    WITHIN `days over which the information is given`
    LEST  BREACH BY `the applicant` BECAUSE "s 4A: a person must not, in giving information under the Act, make a statement knowing it to be false or misleading; fine not exceeding 2 penalty units"

-- s 4B: "The Commissioner, by written notice, may require a person given a remission ... to repay to the Commissioner
-- the amount remitted ... if the Commissioner is satisfied that the person was not entitled to that remission." The
-- notice sets no period. Clock starts on the day the person receives the notice.
GIVEN `the Commissioner has required repayment by written notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Step`
DECIDE `s 4B -- the person given the remission must repay it when the Commissioner requires` IS
    IF `the Commissioner has required repayment by written notice`
    THEN PARTY `the person given the remission`
         MUST  `repay the amount remitted`
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- s 4C, 4E, 4F: the person may object within 60 days after receiving the s 4B notice; the Commissioner "is to
-- determine an objection" and "give written notice" (no period set); the objector may then apply to the Magistrates
-- Court (Administrative Appeals Division) within 60 days after receiving that notice. Clock starts on the day the s 4B
-- notice is received. Not objecting, or not applying for review, is no breach.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Step`
DECIDE `ss 4C, 4E, 4F -- the person may object within 60 days, and then apply for review within 60 days` IS
    PARTY `the person given the remission`
    DO    `lodge a written objection with the Commissioner`
    WITHIN `the days to object under s 4C`
    HENCE (PARTY `the Commissioner`
           MUST  `determine the objection and give written notice`
           HENCE (PARTY `the objector`
                  DO    `apply to the Magistrates Court for a review`
                  WITHIN `the days to apply for review under s 4F`
                  LEST  FULFILLED))
    LEST  FULFILLED
